        "line": 2,
        "text": "id: cor-pa36-category-o-localization"
      },
      {
        "line": 91,
        "text": "3.1 The TDO $\\mathcal D_\\kappa$ is $G$-equivariant by its action-algebroid construction. The diagonal $B$-action therefore makes $\\operatorname{Loc}_\\kappa(V)$ strongly $B$-equivariant; it is coherent by [F4]. Conversely, if $M$ is strongly $B$-equivariant and coherent, its global sections inherit a rational $B$-action. The torus action is a direct sum of integral weight spaces, and the unipotent action makes each $U(\\mathfrak n^+)$-orbit finite-dimensional. By [F4], $\\Gamma M$ is finitely generated over $A_\\kappa$, hence over $U(\\mathfrak g)$, and its central ideal acts by zero because $A_\\kappa$ is the central quotient in [[def-pa36-flag-tdo-and-module]]. Thus $\\Gamma M$ lies in $\\mathcal O_{\\chi_\\kappa}^{\\mathrm{exact}}$. [F3, F4, step 2.1]"
      }
    ]
