        "text": "1.1 The twist parameter is $\\kappa=0$, so $\\langle\\kappa,\\alpha^\\vee\\rangle=0$: it is antidominant and singular under the definitions in [[def-pa36-flag-tdo-and-module]]. The line bundle $\\mathcal O(-1)$ is nonzero and is a $\\mathcal D_0$-module by [F1]. [F1, given]"
      },
      {
        "line": 66,
        "text": "2.1 By [F3], $p_\\alpha:X\\to G/P_\\alpha$ is the map to a point. Hence $p_{\\alpha*}\\mathcal O(-1)=H^0(X,\\mathcal O(-1))=0$, while $\\mathcal O(-1)\\ne0$. The global-sections kernel and the parabolic-pushforward kernel are therefore nonzero, contradicting the refuted assertion. This is the singular Serre-kernel branch, not a counterexample to exactness: the antidominant global-sections functor remains exact by [[thm-pa36-flag-d-affinity]]. [F2, F3, step 1.1, step 1.2] \u220e"
